  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Oxfam-Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights Initiative</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights, initiative - Oxfam-Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights, initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;rsvara och fr&#xe4;mja SRHR f&#xf6;r flickor, kvinnor och transpersoner.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution Promoting Health and Sexual and Reproductive Rights of Maya, Garifuna and Mestizo Adult Women, Young Women, Adolescent Girls and Trans Women in Guatemala, implemented by Oxfam Interm&#xf3;n and eight local partner organizations, during a period of five years. The Swedish contribution to the project is SEK 76,5 million and Oxfam Intermon will contribute with approximately SEK 3,5 million.&#xa0;
The objective of this project is to defend and promote the sexual and reproductive health and rights of girls, women and trans persons in 10 regions in Guatemala. Financially, the Swedish funds allocated to this contribution will be used for the carrying out of trainings on sexual and reproductive rights with girls and women; attention&#xa0; and the creation of platforms where organizations of women can meet and discuss common challenges and solutions; the provision of psychosocial care to survivors of sexual violence; to provide legal assistance and accompaniment in cases of sexual violence; and other activities. 
Additionally, the funds also target young men who have the potential to change the social imaginary and prevent violence against women. This will be achieved through training possesses and through working with young male leaders from grassroot organizations who will, in turn, be able to affect and provide training to other young men.&#xa0; The activities will be implemented by the eight partner organizations and are estimated to benefit a total of more than 62 000 persons, the majority of whom are women.&#xa0; In addition, the project includes advocacy and awareness raising in order to affect institutions and operators working with justice, health and education on SRHR.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programme aims to contribute to the full exercise of sexual and reproductive health and rights for women, youth, and adolescent girls, mainly indigenous and rural to overcome patriarchal discrimination, exclusion and racism and have the opportunity to dignify their lives by addressing gender based cycles of violence and exercising their rights to health and sexual and reproductive rights.

Specific objcetives:

 (i) to defend and promote sexual and reproductive health and rights of girls, women and trans persons in ten regions in Guatemala. (ii) To provide legal assistance, psychosocial care to survivors of violence and sexual violence; this will be achieved through training processes and through working with young male leaders from grass-root organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
